## Why This Is Asked
Tests capability to design production-grade lineage and governance across sources, transforms, and targets, with robust testing for failures.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage modeling across sources, transforms, targets
- Glue Data Catalog + S3 lineage ledger
- Step Functions orchestration, Lake Formation controls
- Schema evolution handling and validation
- End-to-end testing of lineage integrity in ETL runs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: emitLineage(runId, source, transform, target)
function emitLineage(runId, source, transform, target) {
  const entry = {
    run_id: runId,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    source: source,
    transformation: transform,
    target: target,
    status: 'success'
  };
  // Write to lineage ledger in S3
  s3.putObject({
    Bucket: 'lineage-ledger',
    Key: `lineage/${runId}/${Date.now()}.json`,
    Body: JSON.stringify(entry)
  });
  // Update Glue Data Catalog metadata
  glue.updateTable({ ... });
}
```

This approach ensures complete traceability while handling failures gracefully and maintaining data governance through Lake Formation's fencing capabilities.

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical, beginner-appropriate streaming ingestion using common AWS data tooling and basic quality controls.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams for real-time data ingestion
- AWS Glue ETL and Data Catalog for data processing and metadata management
- Parquet format with date-based partitioning for optimized storage and queries
- Simple schema evolution strategies for handling changing data structures
- Data quality checks (required fields, types, nulls)
- CloudWatch alarms and end-to-end testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code to start a Glue job
const glue = new AWS.Glue();
await glue.startJobRun({
  JobName: 'mobile-events-etl',
  Arguments: {
    '--input-stream': 'mobile-app-events',
    '--output-path': 's3://analytics-bucket/events/',
    '--partition-format': 'yyyy/MM/dd'
  }
});
